Practical tips so the plan actually works
Use a dedicated cab with one experienced long-route driver only if the driver is fresh; otherwise, for safety, a two-driver arrangement is better on this kind of intense schedule. This itinerary contains multiple long road stretches totaling well over a thousand kilometers across the three days.

Keep each temple stop to about 45–90 minutes unless you are doing special seva. That is the only way to protect the schedule.

Start before sunrise every day. Temple morning windows and road traffic are the two biggest constraints.

Reconfirm timings if you travel during festival periods, because official HR&CE/temple schedules explicitly note timing changes on special days.


